* s2color.scheme
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* dash translation of Stata's s2color scheme.
*
* Source Stata scheme file : /Applications/StataNow/ado/base/s/scheme-s2color.scheme
*                            (byte-identical under /Applications/Stata/ado/base)
* Stata version            : StataNow 19.5 (MP), born 12 Aug 2026
* Stata #include chain     : s2color (no parent scheme)
* Translated on            : 2026-09-18
* Derived from             : test/fixtures/scheme_truth.json, generated by
*                            scripts/extract_scheme_truth.py from Stata's own
*                            scheme-*.scheme and style/*.style files.
*
* Every colour below is written as a RESOLVED #rrggbb value, not as a Stata
* colour name.  dash's OptionTranslator._COLOR_MAP knows only 72 names, and
* SchemeParser._color() silently returns #000000 for a name it cannot resolve,
* so hex is the only self-contained representation.
*
* Values marked "class default" in the fixture's sources map are recorded here
* under the key dash's SchemeParser actually reads; the comment above each such
* line says how Stata itself supplies the value.
*
* Property categories used by dash SchemeParser:
*   color, symbol, linepattern, linewidth, intensity, gsize, graphsize,
*   symbolsize, clockdir, numstyle
*
* Re-extract and re-check this file whenever Stata is upgraded: the header
* above is only true as of the version and date recorded in it.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

label "s2 color"

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Background and region colors
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
color background      #eaf2f3
color plotregion      #ffffff
color legend          #ffffff
color legend_line     #000000
color grid            #eaf2f3
color major_grid      #eaf2f3
color minor_grid      #505050
color heading         #1e2d53
color axisline        #000000

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Per-plot color cycle (p1-p15), resolved from Stata's color-*.style files
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
color p1      #1a476f
color p2      #90353b
color p3      #55752f
color p4      #e37e00
color p5      #6e8e84
color p6      #c10534
color p7      #938dd2
color p8      #cac27e
color p9      #a0522d
color p10     #7b92a8
color p11     #2d6d66
color p12     #9c8847
color p13     #bfa19c
color p14     #ffd200
color p15     #d9e6eb

* Per-plot line color (for line/connected plots).
* s2color sets no "color p#line"; Stata resolves these through the documented
* p#stub -> pstub -> p# -> p chain, landing on "color p#".  Spelled out here
* because SchemeParser reads p#line by exact key with no fallback.
color p1line   #1a476f
color p2line   #90353b
color p3line   #55752f
color p4line   #e37e00
color p5line   #6e8e84
color p6line   #c10534
color p7line   #938dd2
color p8line   #cac27e
color p9line   #a0522d
color p10line  #7b92a8
color p11line  #2d6d66
color p12line  #9c8847
color p13line  #bfa19c
color p14line  #ffd200
color p15line  #d9e6eb

* Per-plot bar/area fill color (resolves to "color p#", as above)
color p1bar    #1a476f
color p2bar    #90353b
color p3bar    #55752f
color p4bar    #e37e00
color p5bar    #6e8e84
color p6bar    #c10534
color p7bar    #938dd2
color p8bar    #cac27e
color p9bar    #a0522d
color p10bar   #7b92a8
color p11bar   #2d6d66
color p12bar   #9c8847
color p13bar   #bfa19c
color p14bar   #ffd200
color p15bar   #d9e6eb

* Per-plot marker fill color (resolves to "color p#", as above)
color p1mark   #1a476f
color p2mark   #90353b
color p3mark   #55752f
color p4mark   #e37e00
color p5mark   #6e8e84
color p6mark   #c10534
color p7mark   #938dd2
color p8mark   #cac27e
color p9mark   #a0522d
color p10mark  #7b92a8
color p11mark  #2d6d66
color p12mark  #9c8847
color p13mark  #bfa19c
color p14mark  #ffd200
color p15mark  #d9e6eb

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Marker symbol cycle
* s2color declares a single "symbol p circle" class default: every plot in the
* cycle is a circle.  Written out p1-p15 because SchemeParser has no fallback.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
symbol p1     circle
symbol p2     circle
symbol p3     circle
symbol p4     circle
symbol p5     circle
symbol p6     circle
symbol p7     circle
symbol p8     circle
symbol p9     circle
symbol p10    circle
symbol p11    circle
symbol p12    circle
symbol p13    circle
symbol p14    circle
symbol p15    circle

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Line patterns for line/connected plots
* s2color declares a single "linepattern p solid" class default: s2color
* distinguishes series by colour, never by dash pattern.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
linepattern p1line   solid
linepattern p2line   solid
linepattern p3line   solid
linepattern p4line   solid
linepattern p5line   solid
linepattern p6line   solid
linepattern p7line   solid
linepattern p8line   solid
linepattern p9line   solid
linepattern p10line  solid
linepattern p11line  solid
linepattern p12line  solid
linepattern p13line  solid
linepattern p14line  solid
linepattern p15line  solid

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Line widths (Stata linewidth style names; "medium" is .30 Stata units)
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
linewidth p           medium
linewidth major_grid  medium

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Fill intensities
* "intensity area" is not set by any Stata base scheme; s2color resolves it
* through the bare "intensity" class default, which is full.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
intensity p        inten80
intensity bar      full
intensity area     full

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Font sizes (Stata gsize style names, relative units)
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
gsize text          medium
gsize heading       large
gsize axis_title    medsmall
gsize tick_label    medsmall
gsize note          small

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Graph dimensions, in inches (consumed by section 10 for figure proportions)
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
graphsize x  5.5
graphsize y  4

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Default marker size for the p cycle
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
symbolsize p  medium

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Legend placement
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
clockdir legend_position  6
numstyle legend_cols      2

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Major grid switches.  SchemeParser stores these in _props but
* _init_properties() exposes no attribute for them yet; recorded so the
* declared value is available when a consumer lands.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
yesno draw_major_hgrid  no
yesno draw_major_grid   no
